+# Deploying the Tip Jar (static site on IPFS, contract on Base)
+
+Production is a static export (`next build` with `output: "export"`), uploaded to IPFS. The site talks to the real Base chain (8453) through the user's wallet and an Alchemy RPC. No server is involved.
+
+Run all commands from the repo root unless a step says `cd`.
+
+## What the production build configuration does
+
+| Setting | Where | Effect |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true` | `next.config.ts` | `output: "export"` and `trailingSlash: true`, so every route becomes `route/index.html` and IPFS gateways can resolve it. Also `images.unoptimized`. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true` | `scaffold.config.ts` | Target network switches from the local fork (`chains.foundry`) to `chains.base`. The burner wallet is disabled, because it is only enabled for local networks. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` | `utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts` | Absolute `og:image` / `metadataBase`. Without it, previews point at `localhost:3000`. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` | `scaffold.config.ts` | Base RPC. With your own key, Alchemy is tried first. The default shared key would put the public RPC first. |
+| `NODE_OPTIONS=--require ./polyfill-localstorage.cjs` | `packages/nextjs/polyfill-localstorage.cjs` | Node 25+ has a broken global `localStorage` that crashes prerendering. `--require` also reaches Next's build workers. |
+| `scripts/ipfs-preflight.mjs` | runs first in `yarn build:ipfs` | Fails the build if the URL or Alchemy key is missing, or if TipJar is not in `deployedContracts.ts` for chain 8453. |
+
+`yarn build:ipfs` (in `packages/nextjs`) does all of the above: preflight, `rm -rf .next out`, then the build with the env flags.
+
+> `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are embedded in the public bundle. In the Alchemy dashboard, restrict the key to the production domain(s).
+
+## 0. Prerequisite (once per contract version): TipJar deployed on Base
+
+This spends real ETH for gas on Base. Do it from a team keystore, **not** from the anvil keys.
+
+```bash
+yarn account:import                  # or: yarn generate   (creates a Foundry keystore)
+yarn account                         # check the address has ETH on Base
+
+TIP_JAR_OWNER=<team-multisig-or-owner> \
+  yarn deploy --network base --keystore <keystore-name>
+yarn verify --network base           # needs ETHERSCAN_API_KEY in packages/foundry/.env
+```
+
+`yarn deploy --network base` adds a `8453: { TipJar: ... }` entry to `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`. **Commit that file.** The IPFS build reads the Base address from it.
+
+Check the deployment:
+
+```bash
+BASE_RPC="https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/<alchemy-key>"
+JAR=$(awk '/^  8453: \{/{f=1} f&&/address:/{print; exit}' packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts | grep -o '0x[0-9a-fA-F]\{40\}')
+cast call $JAR "usdc()(address)"  --rpc-url $BASE_RPC   # 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913
+cast call $JAR "owner()(address)" --rpc-url $BASE_RPC   # the intended owner
+```
+
+## 1. Build
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://tipjar.<yourname>.eth.link"   # final public URL, https, no trailing slash
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY="<alchemy-key>"
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID="<walletconnect-project-id>" # optional, recommended
+
+yarn build:ipfs
+```
+
+This is equivalent to:
+
+```bash
+node scripts/ipfs-preflight.mjs
+rm -rf .next out
+NODE_OPTIONS='--require ./polyfill-localstorage.cjs' NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true yarn build   # yarn build = eslint + next build
+```
+
+Do not set `NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR=true`. A type error here usually means the Base deployment entry is wrong.
+
+## 2. Verify the build before uploading (still in `packages/nextjs`)
+
+```bash
+# Every route is a directory with index.html (needed for IPFS gateways)
+ls out/index.html out/debug/index.html
+
+# Metadata points at the production URL, not localhost
+grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>' out/index.html
+! grep -rl "localhost:3000" out --include=*.html && echo "no localhost refs"
+
+# The bundle contains the Base TipJar address
+JAR=$(awk '/^  8453: \{/{f=1} f&&/address:/{print; exit}' contracts/deployedContracts.ts | grep -o '0x[0-9a-fA-F]\{40\}')
+grep -rli "${JAR#0x}" out/_next/static/chunks | head -1
+
+# Not stale: output must be newer than the latest source change
+stat -f '%Sm' app/page.tsx app/_components/*.tsx contracts/deployedContracts.ts   # macOS; Linux: stat -c '%y'
+stat -f '%Sm' out/index.html
+
+# Smoke test the exact files that will be uploaded
+python3 -m http.server 8080 --directory out
+# open http://localhost:8080 → header shows Base, connect wallet, feed loads from Base
+```
+
+## 3. Upload
+
+BuidlGuidl IPFS (`bgipfs` is already a devDependency of `packages/nextjs`):
+
+```bash
+# once per machine; the API key comes from https://upload.bgipfs.com
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com -k <BGIPFS_API_KEY>
+
+yarn bgipfs upload out          # prints "CID: <cid>". Record it
+export CID=<cid>
+```
+
+(`yarn ipfs` does build, config init, and upload in one command. The step-by-step version above lets you verify before uploading.)
+
+After any code change the CID **must** change. If it matches the previous deploy, you uploaded a stale `out/`.
+
+## 4. Post-deploy verification
+
+Next.js export uses root-absolute asset paths (`/_next/...`). Test on a **subdomain** gateway, which serves the CID at `/`. This needs a CIDv1 (`bafy…`). If you got a `Qm…` CID, convert it with `ipfs cid base32 $CID` (kubo).
+
+```bash
+GW="https://$CID.ipfs.dweb.link"
+
+# Routes resolve (expect 200 for each)
+for p in / /debug/ /debug; do
+  printf '%s %s\n' "$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -L "$GW$p")" "$p"
+done
+
+# Served content equals the local build
+curl -sL "$GW/" | diff -q - out/index.html && echo "index.html matches"
+
+# A JS chunk loads (assets resolve from root)
+ASSET=$(grep -o '/_next/static/[^"]*\.js' out/index.html | head -1)
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{content_type}\n' "$GW$ASSET"
+
+# Title and OG metadata
+curl -sL "$GW/" | grep -o '<title>[^<]*'
+curl -sL "$GW/" | grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>'
+
+# The BuidlGuidl gateway also serves it
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -L "https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/$CID/"
+```
+
+Manual browser check on `$GW`. Only the last step uses real money: tip a small amount such as $1.
+
+1. The page loads, the title is "USDC Tip Jar", and the header network is Base.
+2. Connect a wallet that is on another chain. The app offers "Switch to Base" and switching works.
+3. The feed and totals load (they are read from the Base TipJar).
+4. Tip 1 USDC: **Approve** shows a spinner and confirms, then **Send tip** confirms. The feed and total update.
+5. Reject a transaction in the wallet. The UI recovers and shows an error toast.
+
+## 5. Point ENS at it (optional; two Ethereum mainnet transactions)
+
+1. `https://app.ens.domains/<yourname>.eth` → Subnames → create `tipjar` (new apps only).
+2. `https://app.ens.domains/tipjar.<yourname>.eth` → Records → Edit → Content Hash: `ipfs://<CID>` → save.
+
+Verify:
+
+```bash
+NAME=tipjar.<yourname>.eth
+MAINNET_RPC="https://eth-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/$NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY"
+RESOLVER=$(cast call 0x00000000000C2e074eC69A0dFb2997BA6C7d2e1e "resolver(bytes32)(address)" $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url $MAINNET_RPC)
+cast call $RESOLVER "contenthash(bytes32)(bytes)" $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url $MAINNET_RPC   # encodes $CID
+
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -L "https://$NAME.link"            # 200 (cache may take 5–15 min)
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -L "https://$NAME.link/debug/"     # 200
+curl -sL "https://$NAME.link" | grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>'   # https://$NAME.link/thumbnail.jpg
+```
+
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` must match the URL you serve from (e.g. `https://tipjar.<yourname>.eth.link`). If you change the domain, rebuild and re-upload.
